    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3410" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arcessītor</span></b> ,
		ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one that calls</i> or <i>fetches</i> another
			(perh. only in the two foll. exs.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nemo arcessitor ex proximo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 5, 6, 45</span></i>
			.—Hence, in judic. lang., <i>an
			accuser</i>, <i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 1, 44</span></i>.</div>
